---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us | EngineerExperiences"
  description="Who writes EngineerExperiences, what is documented here, and how the site itself is built and deployed."
>
  <section class="section">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li>
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="current" aria-current="page">About Us</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>About Us</h1>
      <p>
        EngineerExperiences is my engineering documentation site. I write up the embedded systems,
        firmware and tooling work as I build it, so the reasoning behind a design is captured next to
        the design instead of in a chat window that is lost a week later.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>How EngineerExperiences is built</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Static Astro</h3>
        <p>
          The whole site is pre-rendered with Astro: every project chapter, article part and search
          entry is produced at build time, so there is no application server behind it.
        </p>
        <span class="card-meta">Astro · Markdown content collections · TypeScript</span>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>AWS S3 and CloudFront</h3>
        <p>
          The build is deployed to Amazon S3 on every push and served through CloudFront. GitHub
          Actions authenticates with OIDC and assumes a restricted IAM role, so no AWS access key is
          stored in the repository.
        </p>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <a href="/articles/aws-s3-cloudfront-deployment/">
            Read the deployment series <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>Source code</h3>
        <p>
          The site, the documentation and the deployment workflow live in one public repository, so
          every page can be traced back to the commit that published it. There is no comment section
          here, so corrections, questions and ideas are all welcome as GitHub issues.
        </p>
        <div class="card-footer">
          <a href="https://github.com/isarwar93/documentation-blog/" rel="noreferrer">
            github.com/isarwar93/documentation-blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;·&nbsp;</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/isarwar93/documentation-blog/issues" rel="noreferrer">
            Open an issue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
